# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads (it reads this file, not .dockerignore). The image build needs only these files:
#   container/Dockerfile, container/bootstrap.sh, requirements.txt (and cloudbuild.yaml, which Cloud Build reads).
# Everything else is left out on purpose: a build folder can be several GB, and .env holds real keys.
*
!cloudbuild.yaml
!requirements.txt
!container
container/*
!container/Dockerfile
!container/bootstrap.sh
